# Banter in Foxwillow and the Fields of the Crow (story/banter.gd plays this file only where a place's region is foxwillow): one exchange between two or three companions about what is in
# front of them in one place, gated on that place (`at:`) and on the story's state so a remark never runs ahead of the chapter. Played now and then on entering
# an area, once each; an exchange nobody present can speak comes out empty and is skipped.
# Drafted by Gemini (docs/plans/gemini_companions/), edited; every edit is listed in the README there. Lines are unvoiced until the voice lane reads them.


~ foxwillow_01_rook_cordelia
if name:rook_coldwake and name:cordelia_skein and at:foxwillow and not flag.fw_brawl_a_done
interject name:rook_coldwake: That windmill on the bluff is a wheel of fire, Cordelia, and the town pump just sits there.
interject name:cordelia_skein: That burning hay smells of roasted gourd and char. My six eyes can barely manage the glare.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Pumpkin-headed brawlers in the square, and corn three yards past regulation height.
interject name:cordelia_skein: You haven't inhaled in four minutes, Rook. I suppose it spares your lungs the ash.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Right you are. There's a sigh for the log. Tastes of burnt squash.
endif
-> END

~ foxwillow_02_silas_tobin
if name:silas_vane and name:tobin_hayward and at:foxwillow and flag.fw_brawl_c_done and not flag.raum_slain
interject name:silas_vane: Three bouts cleared, Tobin, and that scarecrow in the bonnet folded at the first pitchfork.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Don't gloat over shoddy stitchwork. And step round that pumpkin head before an ember finds my hem.
interject name:silas_vane: Easy, friend. Not a live spark near William's cart.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Someone stuffed these folk with dry haulm and set them on their own neighbours.
interject name:silas_vane: Bad hand from a marked shoe. Whoever's banking this game out east still owes the town.
endif
-> END

~ fw_windmill_03_delphine_lucan
if name:delphine_ravelle and name:lucan_houndstooth and at:fw_windmill and not flag.fw_mill_done
interject name:delphine_ravelle: That great cog overhead sounds like stage machinery cranked by a stagehand with a grudge.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Hush, Barnaby, it's only timber groaning, not thunder. Keep behind me, if you please, Delphine.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Your Foolishness stopped punning at the flour dust. When he goes quiet, I mind my seams.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Charred straw and scorched grease on these steps. And poor Liza Sawyer looks half-choked.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Then let's climb before the roof comes down. I won't be buried in meal like a penny sack.
endif
-> END

~ fw_store_04_tobin_delphine
if name:tobin_hayward and name:delphine_ravelle and at:fw_store and not flag.raum_slain
interject name:tobin_hayward: Back from that rubble, Delphine. My mice are scrambling, and the heat's blistering the shelves.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: I'm felt and sawdust under this velvet, darling. I've no wish to go up like a cheap curtain.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Look there in the cinders. A banjo's neck, still whole.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Someone tuned it for a last number. Even my patron hasn't a joke for a snapped string.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Come away from the embers. One scorched thread and the whole sleeve unravels.
endif
-> END

~ fw_library_05_cordelia_tobin
if name:cordelia_skein and name:tobin_hayward and at:fw_library and not flag.fw_librarian_done
interject name:cordelia_skein: Look at these stacks of books, Tobin. Not a thought for ventilation. The glue's gone positively syrupy.
interject name:tobin_hayward: That's damp-rot in the rag paper, creeping up the spines like canker in an apple loft.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Agnes Fennel seems absorbed in her catalogue. Her pulse is remarkably brisk for a librarian.
interject name:tobin_hayward: A good ledger smells of linseed and flax, not tallow and shut windows.
interject name:cordelia_skein: I would never leave an unindexed stain in another woman's collection, Tobin.
endif
-> END

~ fw_circle_06_lucan_tobin
if name:lucan_houndstooth and name:tobin_hayward and at:fw_circle and not flag.raum_slain
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Good heavens, Tobin. Every stalk flattened to the millimetre. And that figure in the centre unsettles me.
interject name:tobin_hayward: You couldn't bend stalks this thick with a heavy roller. Something foul fed the root.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Barnaby just yipped, and there's no dropped kettle corn here. The air tastes of cold iron.
interject name:tobin_hayward: That's Virgil standing in the rows. No farmhand tied the twine at his joints.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Eight out of ten for symmetry, if my hackles would lie flat long enough to write it down.
endif
-> END

~ fw_maze_j1_07_silas_delphine
if name:silas_vane and name:delphine_ravelle and at:fw_maze_j1 and not flag.raum_slain
interject name:silas_vane: Hear the crows, Delphine? Every one of 'em cawing on the off-beat, like a rigged wheel.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Heckling from the cheap seats. And Your Foolishness is mimicking them in my ear.
interject name:silas_vane: The wind through these stalks is whistling straight across my ribs. Cold as a blade.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Your shadow's lagging half a step behind you, Silas. And it keeps looking up at the tassels.
interject name:silas_vane: Let it look. While I can shuffle one-handed, the house hasn't closed the walls on us.
endif
-> END

~ foxwillow_08_silas_lucan
if name:silas_vane and name:lucan_houndstooth and at:foxwillow and flag.raum_slain
interject name:silas_vane: Raum's down, the fires are dying, and I just chalked one very large tally inside my ribs.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: A prime example of rural malice, Silas. I'm gladder to see the townsfolk breathing clean air.
interject name:silas_vane: Even the smoke smells like plain wet timber again.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Some still stare east, as if the stalks might march back. A town takes a while to unlearn the dark.
interject name:silas_vane: Tell Barnaby he can stop shaking, friend. The fire on the bluff has cashed in its chips.
endif
-> END
